cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Gen X-ray: training an X-ray foreign-object detector on Diffusion-synthesized images only"
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Jeonghwan
    affiliation: Independent researcher
repository-code: "https://github.com/sinkei9456/gen-xray"
license: AGPL-3.0
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
keywords:
  - X-ray inspection
  - foreign object detection
  - synthetic training data
  - diffusion model
  - YOLO
  - food packaging
abstract: >-
  Food-packaging X-ray images carry inspection-machine marks drawn around every
  foreign object, so a detector cannot be trained on the real images. Gen X-ray
  uses 500 labeled images only as material, trains a conditional Diffusion model
  to draw bags and sticks, inserts real defect patches and drawn shapes following
  X-ray attenuation, and trains YOLO26s on 5,000 synthetic images. The detector
  reaches F1 0.995 on 1,870 real test images never used for training or
  threshold selection.
